  {
    "id": "doc_tkdl_botanical_compendium_chunk_4",
    "document": "Ocimum sanctum (Tulsi / Holy Basil): Virya is Ushna (warming). Rasa is Katu and Tikta. Highly efficacious for Kasa (cough), Shwasa (bronchial asthma), and Vishama Jwara (intermittent viral fevers). Contains eugenol, ursolic acid, and rosmarinic acid.\nTinospora cordifolia (Guduchi / Giloy / Amrita): Classical Tridosha-hara (balances all three doshas Vata, Pitta, Kapha). Virya is Ushna. Rasa is Tikta and Kashaya.\nSpecial Action: Rasayana (immunomodulatory, stimulates macrophage phagocytosis), Jwaraghna (antipyretic), Yakrit-plihodara hara (hepatoprotective).\nPrior Art Defense: Classical preparations like Guduchi Kwatha, Samsamani Vati, and Sanjeevani Vati are documented in the Ayurvedic Formulary of India (AFI Part 1) and are protected from wrongful domestic and international patents under Section 3(p).",
